VIEWERS APPLAUD THANDO

@FransShadung: I never thought I’d say this, but I’m so proud of Thando for standing up for her mother.

@TweetsbyMOD: Yesss, Thando! Defending your mother like that is exactly what a daughter should do. You can have issues with someone without dragging them for being unmarried. That part was unnecessary. She’s standing on business, and I respect it.

@NomceboMasilel2: Thando is standing on business, and I’m here for it. I love that she’s defending her mother. Reprimanding someone is one thing, but belittling her and calling her names because she’s unmarried is uncalled for.

@MrSmegOfficial: Thando is defending her mother in her absence. That’s true love.



@_FentseM: Thando is addressing things with a firmer tone.

@makatla_mandisa: I love how Thando is being outspoken and defending her mother; she has grown.

@BonoTshivhidzo: I love how Thando is standing up for her mother. It’s time. The Dlamukas are very disrespectful towards her mom.

@BonoTshivhidzo: We sometimes think Thando can’t see what’s happening, and tonight is one of those days where we are all proud of her for standing up for herself and her mother.

‘AINT NOTHING LIKE A MAMA’S LOVE’

Freedman Grove sings, “Ain’t nothing like a mama’s love,” and Thando’s mother has consistently embodied the sentiment behind that lyric.

One unforgettable scene was when she confronted her son-in-law, Siyacela Dlamuka, shortly after the young couple welcomed their first child.

Thando’s mother was upset that Siyacela allegedly mistreated her daughter, such as forcing her to prepare food for him despite being pregnant.

Many viewers admired Nokuthula’s strength and bravery for standing up for her daughter.
